      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Analyzing congressional testimony requires examining the precise phrasing used by the official versus the context of the questions asked. If the official consistently used vague language or non-answers when pressed specifically on intelligence failures, it leans toward deliberate obfuscation. However, if the evasiveness was triggered by specific requests for classified source material, his claims of protecting national security likely have a legitimate legal basis under established privilege. You must compare his linguistic patterns against the legal standard for withholding information in that specific committee.",
